# Trivy ignore file
# This file contains vulnerabilities and security issues to ignore during Trivy scans

# Ignore low severity vulnerabilities in development dependencies
# Format: CVE-YYYY-NNNN

# Example: Ignore specific CVE in development tools
# CVE-2023-12345

# Ignore vulnerabilities in test files
# These are typically not included in production builds
**/test/**
**/tests/**
**/__tests__/**
**/*.test.js
**/*.test.ts
**/*.spec.js
**/*.spec.ts

# Ignore vulnerabilities in configuration files that are not deployed
**/.eslintrc.*
**/jest.config.*
**/vitest.config.*
**/tsconfig.json
**/.prettierrc.*

# Ignore vulnerabilities in documentation files
**/README.md
**/CHANGELOG.md
**/*.md

# Ignore known false positives (add specific CVEs as needed)
# CVE-2023-XXXXX  # Example: False positive in development dependency